4. What the Agent Must Build
A) server.js — Main Server File
    • Initialize Express app and listen on PORT from env
    • GET / — health check route that returns 200 OK (used by cron-job.org)
    • GET /status — returns uptime, last email sent time, total emails sent
    • POST /send-email — manually trigger an email send via API call
    • Initialize node-cron with the schedule from CRON_SCHEDULE env variable
    • On cron trigger: fetch recipient list from InsForge DB, send emails, log results

B) Email Function
    • Use Nodemailer with Gmail SMTP transport
    • Credentials loaded from EMAIL and EMAIL_PASS environment variables
    • Support single recipient or array of recipients
    • After each send: log to InsForge DB with timestamp, recipient, status
    • Include try/catch with at least 1 retry on failure

C) InsForge Database
    • Connect using InsForge Postgres client (@insforge/client or pg library)
    • Table: email_logs — columns: id, recipient, subject, sent_at, status
    • Table: recipients — columns: id, email, name, active
    • On startup: check DB connection and log success or failure

D) .env File Structure
EMAIL=yourgmail@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASS=your_16_char_app_password
CRON_SCHEDULE=0 9 * * *
INSFORGE_URL=your_insforge_connection_string
PORT=3000


5. Gmail SMTP Setup (Important)
Gmail requires an App Password — NOT your regular Gmail password. Here is how to get it:

    1. Go to myaccount.google.com
    2. Click Security in the left menu
    3. Enable 2-Step Verification if not already on
    4. Search for App Passwords at the top
    5. Select Mail as the app and your device
    6. Copy the 16-character password generated
    7. Paste it into EMAIL_PASS in your .env file

⚠️  Never use your real Gmail password — it will not work and is a security risk.


