7. Deployment Steps on Render.com
Step 1 — Prepare the Code
    8. Create server.js with all logic
    9. Create .env file locally (NEVER push to GitHub)
    10. Create .gitignore — add .env and node_modules
    11. Run npm init -y and install all packages
    12. Test locally: node server.js — confirm it works
    13. Push to a GitHub repository

Step 2 — Deploy on Render
    14. Go to dashboard.render.com
    15. Click + New then select Web Service
    16. Connect your GitHub repository
    17. Set Build Command: npm install
    18. Set Start Command: node server.js
    19. Add all environment variables in the Render Environment tab
    20. Click Deploy and wait for green status
    21. Copy the live URL (e.g. https://your-app.onrender.com)

Step 3 — Set Up Keep Alive (cron-job.org)
    22. Go to cron-job.org and create a free account
    23. Click Create Cronjob
    24. Set URL to your Render server URL (the / health check route)
    25. Set schedule to every 10 minutes
    26. Enable the cron job
    27. Your server now stays awake all day — never sleeps


