9. Critical Rules for the Agent
    • NEVER push .env to GitHub — always use Render's environment variables dashboard
    • The GET / route MUST return HTTP 200 — this is what keeps the server alive via cron-job.org
    • Use Gmail App Password ONLY — regular Gmail passwords will not work with SMTP
    • All email sending must be wrapped in try/catch with retry logic
    • Log every email event (success or failure) to InsForge email_logs table
    • Do NOT shut down n8n until the new server is fully tested and confirmed working
    • Use async/await throughout — no callbacks


10. Questions Agent Must Clarify Before Starting
    • What exact workflows are running in n8n right now? Please list them all
    • What is the exact email schedule? (e.g. 9 AM daily? Multiple times per day?)
    • How many recipients are there and are they stored somewhere already?
    • What is the email content — fixed template or dynamic per recipient?
    • Is there any webhook or external trigger in n8n that also needs to be replicated?
    • Should n8n run in parallel during testing or be shut down immediately?


